ull}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change pushed to Gerrit: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2451 (commit ed5d973a1644, Change-Id I21e56c9…).\n\n- Plan passed plan-review (signed under the MCP signing env; claim validated it same-env).\n- Worktree `guard-eval-71b5` off origin/main (93ca753). SKILL.md was unchanged vs origin/main between my edit base and tip, so the Step-7 item-1 flip applied cleanly; `structural-guards.md` added new.\n- Local gates green: `make lint`; frontmatter check; and the skill contract tests (`test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py`, `test_skill_shared_sync.py`, `test_check_skill_frontmatter.py`, `test_check_docs_index.py`) — 49 passed. `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` → OK.\n\nAwaiting `LLM-Review +1` + `Verified +1`; will Submit once both are green, then close (not before Verified +1 per policy).","timestamp":1788134535203357423}],"created_at":1788132711016040431,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4a00b314-17c0-4086-8ade-7370bd6d97a3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dff2-9c38-c454-4daa"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md` Step 7, Axis 1 \"Class review\" item 1 (introduced by story dff2-9c38-c454-4daa) **unconditionally** mandates that every confirmed sibling class add \"one criterion asserting a structural check over the class (a construct-uniqueness guard, or an equivalent that fails if a new instance appears)\". Mandating a structural guard for *every* class that has >= 1 sibling over-produces guards: it invites CI bloat, standing maintenance burden, and change-detector checks for classes whose re-entry risk a plain regression test already covers. The skill has no guidance for *when* a guard is warranted or *how* to design one that survives refactors and stays portable.\n\nThis follow-on (requested by the operator this session) converts that unconditional mandate into a bright-line evaluation, backed by a new conditionally-loaded companion prompt, `structural-guards.md`, mirroring how `test-design.md` and `llm-behavioral-taxonomy.md` are loaded on demand.\n\n## Scope (documentation only -- no code, no ticket-system change)\n\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/structural-guards.md` (NEW) -- the companion prompt.\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md` -- Step 7 Axis-1 item 1 flips from the unconditional guard mandate to a decision routed through `structural-guards.md`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Step 7 item 1 contains no unconditional structural-check mandate; it routes the decision through `structural-guards.md`. Verified by reading item 1 and by `tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py` returning exit 0.\n- [ ] Step 7 item 1 still requires one acceptance-criterion checkbox per confirmed sibling naming its path and symbol. Verified by reading item 1.\n- [ ] `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/structural-guards.md` is present. Verified by `test -f`.\n- [ ] `structural-guards.md` opens with a header naming what it governs and its load points (rebar-debug Step 7 Axis 1; rebar-implement). Verified by reading the header.\n- [ ] `structural-guards.md` states the WHEN decision as numbered questions phrased as affirmative tests. Verified by reading the \"does this class earn a guard\" section.\n- [ ] `structural-guards.md` contains a portability table mapping bug shape to guard shape across at least four enforcement layers. Verified by reading the table.\n- [ ] `structural-guards.md` enumerates the design properties as affirmative statements (match on structure not text; carry intent inline; binary and blocking; survive refactor; ship a true-negative). Verified by reading the properties section.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` returns exit 0 and `tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py` returns exit 0 (the new companion needs no frontmatter and is not a shared-synced file). Verified by running each.\n\n## Test plan\n\nDocumentation change. Run: `python scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py`; `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py tests/unit/test_check_skill_frontmatter.py`; `make lint`. No runtime behavior changes.\n\n## Attribution\n\nAdditive skill enhancement, not a defect fix -- it evolves the Step-7 directive that story dff2-9c38-c454-4daa shipped. Relates-to dff2 and its epic e71b (bug-trend program: debug-skill upgrades).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/structural-guards.md","reason":"NEW companion prompt: bright-line WHEN questions + non-brittle HOW-to-design properties, portable across stacks"},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md","reason":"Step 7 Axis-1 item 1: flip unconditional guard mandate to an evaluation gated on structural-guards.md"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","dff2-9c38-c454-4daa"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"511f37d7-eba1-427b-87d9-494dd711b8f6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["rebar-debug","skill","structural-guards"],"ticket_id":"71b5-1ceb-131a-422d","ticket_type":"task","title":"rebar-debug Step 7: gate the class structural-guard on an evaluation, add structural-guards.md companion","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["374a8a11-ab39-4d16-b107-779d6f5ae2fb","b34f59da-9ecd-40b2-a2dc-8b5ab0495466","4a00b314-17c0-4086-8ade-7370bd6d97a3","88745269-6bc5-4db0-acb4-cb1e3dddb6ef","7a59aeef-622b-40e4-8de8-48e80795cd26","511f37d7-eba1-427b-87d9-494dd711b8f6","65530743-e850-4abb-b269-0b18eb66ff19","79e61b3b-3353-4612-a